# Q-05: Caddy reverse proxy for production.
# APP_HOST is REQUIRED (docker-compose.prod.yml fails fast at `compose
# config` time without it). API_HOST is required too, unless you use the
# single-hostname alternative below — never leave both unset: both blocks
# would resolve to `localhost` and Caddy refuses to start with
# "duplicate site address".
# Example: APP_HOST=app.example.com API_HOST=api.example.com
# Caddy obtains/renews TLS automatically via ACME (ports 80/443 must be open
# and both DNS A records must point at this host before first boot).
# APP_TLS_EMAIL is the ACME account email (optional but recommended).
#
# Alternative: serve both from one hostname — comment out the api block, set
# only APP_HOST, and let the Next.js same-origin /api proxy route
# (frontend/app/api/[...path]/route.ts, reads API_INTERNAL_URL per request)
# forward to the API. One hostname = no CORS/Cookie-SameSite split concerns
# (keep COOKIE_SAMESITE=lax in .env).

{$APP_HOST:localhost} {
	tls {$APP_TLS_EMAIL:}
	reverse_proxy web:3000
}

{$API_HOST:localhost} {
	tls {$APP_TLS_EMAIL:}
	reverse_proxy api:4000
}
